{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 2, :comments ["And the woman conceived — at the time of Pharaoh's decree to cast the males into the Nile." "And she bore a son and saw him, that he was good, and she hid him — for the commentator to explain 'because she saw that he was good, she hid him' is false, for all mothers have compassion on their newborns. Rather, one must explain ותרא as in וירא אלהים את כל אשר עשה והנה טוב מאד — He scrutinized and examined all His deeds and all His works that He had done, whether anything needed correcting, and behold, all were fine and properly formed. So too here: because Moshe was born at the end of six months, as we find with Shmuel, who was born at the turn of the year — two seasons and two days. And therefore she was able to hide him for three months, for the Egyptians would inspect pregnant women at the end of nine months; therefore she examined him at the hour of birth to see whether he was a stillbirth, so that she would not trouble herself with hiding him, and she saw that he was good and fine — for his signs were complete, his hair and his nails, as we learned in Yevamot — and she knew that he was viable." "And she hid him three months — until the end of nine months, which is the time of delivery for most women. And when they came to inspect her, she said to them: it was a stillbirth, or the Egyptians cast it into the Nile."], :book :exodus, :voice :rashbam, :lang :en, :chapter 2, :notes {1 "The bracketed letter [מ] in 'משקר הוא' appears to belong to the word שקר ('false'), not the preposition מ ('from'); translated accordingly."}, :source-witnesses [{"versionTitle" "Sefaria community Hebrew (PD)", "language" "he"}], :timestamp "2026-07-30T14:41:04.453678116Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}